holzBar links no third-party package; the adapted projects and their licenses are
listed in the app under Settings, About, Acknowledgements.

As required by section 5 of the GPL-3.0, this is a modified version of Ice.
Changes made in holzBar since forking on 2026-10-01 include:

  - A macOS 27 backend, contributed upstream by RabenkoYevhenii in
    https://github.com/jordanbaird/Ice/pull/995 and merged into holzBar.
  - Resetting a stale permission from the permissions window.
  - Distribution through Homebrew; the Sparkle updater is removed.
  - New features: layout profiles, groups, spacers, placement of new items,
    per-display holzBar Shelf, notch overflow, black menu bar, rounded screen
    corners, automation rules, URL commands, settings export and import.
  - More features up to 0.0.8: scripts and profile hooks, widgets, layout
    snapshots, a Touch ID or password lock for hidden items, shared profiles, a
    clean-up assistant, copy diagnostics, menu bar styles and the cooperation
    with macOS 27's own overflow button.
  - More features up to 1.0.0: the notch hub with its modules (Timers,
    Calendar, Live activities, File drop, Display controls, Accessory alerts,
    Notifications and Now Playing), a count badge on the icon, the built-in
    items and app launchers, and a layout editor that draws first.
  - No menu bar item XPC service and no helper app. One signed library, loaded
    by Apple's perl, for the optional Read all apps of Now Playing, and one
    entitlement (Calendar). Translated into nineteen languages besides English
    (machine-made).
  - A new name (holzBar, bundle identifier com.holzcloud.holzBar), logo, app
    icon and menu bar icon; settings of Ice are imported on first launch.

The full history of changes is available in this repository's Git history.

